      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We studied the analgesic effect of olipiphate, a product of lignin, against writhing provoked by intraperitoneal injection of acetic acid. Paracetamol was used as the reference drug. Both agents dose-dependently decreased the number of motor reactions caused by the irritant. Olipiphate possessed analgesic activity and efficiency comparable with those of paracetamol, but produced a more long-lasting effect."},
